// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Adapted from Goblint tests/regression/82-widen/06-post_loop1.c: b
// accumulates max(b, a) over a counted loop a < 5, so b == 4 on exit.
// Goblint expects b < 5 only under solvers.td3.widen_gas 6, which delays
// widening long enough for a to settle at [0,4] and b along with it.
//
// Voblint answers UNKNOWN. Mechanism: the head widens both variables on
// the first revisit; narrowing recovers a = [0,5] at the head because
// the guard a < 5 cuts a, but no guard mentions b, and b := max(b, a)
// reads b's own widened value back, so every re-evaluation of the body
// returns [0,+inf] for b and the head keeps it (measured: b = [0,+inf]
// at the head and the check). Narrowing descends only through a guard,
// never through an accumulator's self-dependency.
// Solver-invariant across join, per-origin, warrow, warrow-per-origin.
void main() {
  b := 0;
  a := 0;
  while (a < 5) {
    b := max(b, a);
    a := a + 1
  };
  __voblint_check(b < 5) // UNKNOWN
}
